// {"files":[{"path":"\\\\?\\C:\\Users\\danie\\OneDrive\\github-repos\\drosemann\\README.md","hunks":[{"oldStart":35,"oldLines":7,"newStart":35,"newLines":7,"lines":[" For storage I ended up with OneDrive 365 Basic with 100 GB for 2 euros a month, after years of being convinced I'd never give Microsoft a cent, until the Windows and Samsung integration won me over."," Speed doesn't matter much to me, and if OneDrive ever offers a 500 GB cold archive tier on very slow old hard drives for one or two euros a month, I'd be the first customer, and I'd probably store all my photos there too since 100 GB is easily enough for me."," I never actually needed it, since I never used more than two or three GB, but now I just upload 30 GB so I can say I use it.","-Long term I don't want just any job, I want to build my own thing and found an IT company for hosting, infrastructure and IT consulting, based on infra-pilot.","+Long term I don't want just any job, I want to build my own thing and found an IT company for hosting, infrastructure and IT consulting, based on infra-pilot (https://github.com/drosemann/infra-pilot)."," I want scalable cloud solutions instead of generic root servers, built on pure Docker and KVM."," I also want to buy an old house, make it smart the cheap way, and document all of it on YouTube."," I want to share what I learn, so a YouTube channel about IT and hosting is planned."]}]}]}
